<!--
This file contains sample/specimen control information for S1000D generation. 
It will almost certainly require some small modifications for your production S1000D system.

Note that S1000D control information can be defined in three different places:

1) as properties of a diagram
2) as properties of the project
3) In this file ('CONTROL.XML')

The system reads each property in order first from the diagram, then  the design, project, then this file. 
Any property defined in a diagram takes precedence over property defined in the design.  
Any property defined in a design takes precedence over property defined in the project.  
Thirdly any property is not defined by the project will be read from this file. 
Finally any property not defined in any of the three places will result in an error.

This file format is chosen here to make it very easy to insert these records directly into Capital XML 
files  (it uses the same format,)

The Capital system is open ended and can be used for many types of smart system generation, not just S1000D.
The only requirement for a property to be recognised by this system is that the property begins with an uppercase
'S1000D'.  Hence you are free to use completely different property names even for a S1000D system.  We would not 
recommend that, it could cause support issues and also require that you rewrite the mapping files. However, 
it can be used very easily add additional properties interpreted during generation and mapping.


Capital Property	            Meaning   					   Relavance      Example           

S1000D.DC                     DisassemblyCode                  DMC            029  
S1000D.DCV                    DisassemblyCodeVariant           DMC            A  
S1000D.IC                     InformationCode                  DMC            000  
S1000D.ICV                    InformationCodeVariant           DMC            Y  
S1000D.ISSNUM                 IssueNumber2Digitcode            ICN            02  
S1000D.MI                     ModelIdentificationCode          DMC&ICN        S1000DLIGHTING              
S1000D.ORG                    OriginatorCodeNCAGE              ICN            AABCC  
S1000D.RPC                    ResponsiblePartnerCompany        ICN            Y  
S1000D.SDC                    SystemDifferenceCode             ICN            AAA  
S1000D.SNS_LC                 LearnCode                        DMC&ICN        T45 
S1000D.SNS_LEC                LearnEventCode                   DMC&ICN        C 
S1000D.subSystemCode          SNSSubSystemCode                 DMC&ICN        3                
S1000D.systemCode             SNSMainCode                      DMC&ICN        12               
S1000D.subSubSystemCode       SNSSubSubSystemCode              DMC&ICN        4                
S1000D.SEC                    SecurityClassification           ICN            1  
S1000D.SQ                     SequentialNumber                 ICN            01  
S1000D.VAR                    IllustrationVariance             ICN            A
S1000D.assyCode               AssemblyCode                     dmI            56              
S1000D.ACV                    AssemblyCodeVariant              ???            G
S1000D.LC                     LocationCode                     dmI            R

see note at end referring to the CLC codes.  
S1000D.CLC            connectionListClass              always per device - NOT read from the project, design, or this file

Typically we would expect  systemCode+subSystemCode+subSubSystemCode+assyCode lto be  12+3+4+56


-->
<S1000DControlInfo>

    <!-- To be read by some S1000D tools such as Arbortext tools each module 
	we have to insert some extra 'DOCTYPE'  text at the beginning of the XML for the DMC.
	In this 'liturgical' section - and in this section alone - we use: 
	   $ICN$ to stand for the full calculated ICN 
	   $DMC$ to stand for the full calculated DMC 
    The data in the liturgy  should begin immediately after the Cdata marker.
	Please do not adjust the DOCTYPE liturgy stated here unless you fully understand the implications, S1000D
	documentation systems are not tolerant of variation or mistakes, 

Note that part of the liturgy the 'LiturgyRepeat' is repeated for each included diagram to create something like:

<!DOCTYPE dmodule [
<!ENTITY ICN-21-AAA-21-40-00-A-S4080-01-1-001-1-TC   SYSTEM "ICN-21-AAA-21-40-00-A-S4080-01-1-001-1-TC.cgm" NDATA cgm>
<!ENTITY ICN-21-AAA-21-40-00-A-S4080-02-1-001-1-TC   SYSTEM "ICN-21-AAA-21-40-00-A-S4080-02-1-001-1-TC.cgm" NDATA cgm>
<!ENTITY ICN-21-AAA-21-40-00-A-S4080-03-1-001-1-TC   SYSTEM "ICN-21-AAA-21-40-00-A-S4080-03-1-001-1-TC.cgm" NDATA cgm>
<!ENTITY ICN-21-AAA-21-40-00-A-S4080-04-1-001-1-TC   SYSTEM "ICN-21-AAA-21-40-00-A-S4080-04-1-001-1-TC.cgm" NDATA cgm>
<!NOTATION cgm PUBLIC "-//USA-DOD//NOTATION Computer Graphics Metafile//EN">
]> 
	
	-->
    <LiturgyHeader><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--Arbortext, Inc., 1988-2013, v.4002-->
<!DOCTYPE dmodule [
]]>	
    </LiturgyHeader>
    <LiturgyRepeat><![CDATA[
<!ENTITY $ICN$   SYSTEM "$ICN$.cgm" NDATA cgm>]]>	
    </LiturgyRepeat>
    <LiturgyFooter><![CDATA[<!NOTATION cgm PUBLIC "-//USA-DOD//NOTATION Computer Graphics Metafile//EN">
]>]]>	
    </LiturgyFooter>
    <!--
	
	In the  default section we have chosen to supply all the defaults with a '!'  character -  that means they 
	will need to be present in the project files and that a "!" charcater in a file name of refernce is an error .  
	There is  no necessity to use the system in this way.  An alternative approach is to define real constants at 
	this level.  Initially, and for small projects, that will work quite well. However for larger projects it can 
	become difficult, even after examination of the log files, to understand why certain designs or diagrams have constants taken from this file.
	
	
	-->
